# Operation Modes

Standard operation supports most workloads out of the box. For port scanning, choose between default accuracy or high-throughput performance.

## Default

Use the default mode for interactive sessions — SSH, RDP, database connections — and general traffic. No flags required.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}

## Port Scanning

### Default — accurate

Before completing each TCP handshake, the exit node is probed to check port reachability. If a port is closed, a proper RST is sent back — so nmap correctly reports `closed`. No special configuration needed, nmap just works.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}

```
$ nmap 10.65.65.65
PORT     STATE  SERVICE
22/tcp   open   ssh
80/tcp   closed http
443/tcp  open   https
```

### Fast — less accurate

Skips the probe, removing the per-connection round-trip overhead for significantly higher throughput. The tradeoff: without the probe, RSTs can't be sent for closed ports — so nmap will report them as `filtered` rather than `closed`. Precise port state analysis is no longer reliable; better suited to masscan-style tools where throughput matters more than accuracy.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443 --fast" /%}

```
$ nmap 10.65.65.65
PORT     STATE    SERVICE
22/tcp   open     ssh
80/tcp   filtered http
443/tcp  open     https
```
